WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.709
Welcome to MX Terminal.

00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:07.419
Every African market, one terminal.

00:00:08.569 --> 00:00:14.881
Start at the sign-in screen.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:21.193
The quickest way in is Continue with Google.

00:00:21.193 --> 00:00:27.506
If you would rather use an email address, choose Create Account, enter your email and a password of at least eight characters, and you are in.

00:00:28.056 --> 00:00:36.381
Once you are in, this is the board.

00:00:36.381 --> 00:00:44.707
One thousand and twenty five listed companies, across Johannesburg, Lagos, Nairobi and Cairo.

00:00:44.707 --> 00:00:53.032
Everything on this screen is end of day, priced at the last close, and the whole layout is one screen, with no windows to arrange.

00:00:53.582 --> 00:01:00.241
Across the top runs the tape: the index level for the market you are on, then every security with its price and its move on the day.

00:01:00.241 --> 00:01:06.899
It scrolls on its own.

00:01:07.449 --> 00:01:12.290
Down the left is the watchlist for that market.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:17.131
Every listed company, its logo, its code, the price and the day's move.

00:01:17.131 --> 00:01:21.972
Click any name to pull it up.

00:01:22.522 --> 00:01:36.965
On the right, the market rail summarises the session: how many rose and how many fell, then the top gainers, the top losers, and the most actively traded names.

00:01:37.515 --> 00:01:44.364
MX Terminal is keyboard first.

00:01:44.364 --> 00:01:51.213
The command line sits at the top.

00:01:51.213 --> 00:01:58.062
Type a ticker to pull up a company, a panel code to change the view, or an exchange name to switch markets.

00:01:58.062 --> 00:02:04.911
You can combine them: type M T N, space, F I N, and you get MTN's financials.

00:02:05.461 --> 00:02:11.753
Heatmap gives you the whole market at a glance.

00:02:11.753 --> 00:02:18.046
Each block is a sector, sized by weight and coloured by the day's move.

00:02:18.046 --> 00:02:24.338
Green is up, red is down, and an empty tile means that stock simply did not trade.

00:02:24.888 --> 00:02:40.080
Financials pulls the income statement, the balance sheet and the cash flow straight out of each company's own filings, with the reporting periods side by side, and the ratios worked out underneath.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:49.774
News is one wire for each market.

00:02:49.774 --> 00:02:58.917
Press headlines, the regulator wire, and corporate actions, dividends and book closures, all in a single list, with a ticker chip on anything tied to a company.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:09.796
The screener filters every listed equity by sector, by price, by change and by volume, and exports what you find.

00:03:09.796 --> 00:03:20.124
Alongside it sit commodities, bonds, foreign exchange, time and sales, and analyst ratings.

00:03:20.674 --> 00:03:27.008
If you want any of this in writing, the full guide lives on the site.

00:03:27.008 --> 00:03:33.342
Open mutxriterminal dot com, and click Guide in the top navigation.

00:03:33.892 --> 00:03:44.545
Every panel code, every keyboard shortcut, and a written walk through of each panel is on that page, alongside this tour.

00:03:45.095 --> 00:03:48.707
That is MX Terminal.

00:03:48.707 --> 00:03:52.319
Every African market, one terminal.

